BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Generations (2020)
DTSTART:20260320T020000Z
DTEND:20260320T033500Z
DTSTAMP:20260320T020000Z
UID:jfYEq3gFQE
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 77 mins (1h17m)\n\nPresented by Mount Analogue • 
 Art + Cinema with Tacoma Art Museum and Seattle Documentary AssociationCom
 posed of scenes of coal power plants and their surrounding environments\, 
 Generations was filmed throughout the United States between 2017 to 2019. 
 The film consists of twelve static single-shot tableaus depicting people d
 oing everyday activities while living in the shadow of massive power-gener
 ating stations.Post-film Q&A with director Lynne Siefert and Tacoma Art Mu
 seum curator Ellen Ito.World Premiere at the 70th Berlin International Fil
 m Festival"a rigorous wonder of sound design and interpretative possibilit
 y" — MUBI\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/cinema/in-theaters/generations\n\nEsti
 mated start: 19:15
LOCATION:SIFF Film Center\, 305 Harrison Street
END:VEVENT
